a former emergency room doctor  screenwriter Masson sagai one an a  double acp Image Award for bail she made  her writing debut on the secret laughter  of women and adapted Zora Neale  Hurston's Their Eyes Were Watching God  presenting the award to vigil Jame is  Miss answer guy  [Applause]  good evening we've spoken a lot about  what makes her Nichols fellowship  finalist I think you might as well ask  what makes a writer what do we look for  there's talent and an authentic voice  and I can't deny my pride in having this  Nigerian subject dealt with by a  Nigerian writer  there's craft there's practice and  there's experience but what sets these  scripts apart for me is courage the  courage of a writer from the outset we  write as a subject to so much received  wisdom being told what kinds of stories  sell what characters we need to make it  watchable what kind of actors will be  cast in order to make the script  bankable what will sell overseas over  and over again we are invited to limit  ourselves with this received wisdom it  takes a writer to say no to listen to  the received wisdom with respect and yet  in the end go your own way because this  is the story you want to tell vigil Chi  Mei is courageous because she did just  that born in Nigeria her parents  emigrated to the United States where and  she was brought up in use in Houston  living in New York she now works as a  schoolteacher conventional wisdom says  that all of us want to send our children  here to school after all there are  people who want to build walls to keep  us out there are so many of us and yet  vigil sent her son from New York back to  Nigeria to school I asked her why  he said I wanted a place for him where a  black boy is seen as a king her script  bring back girl  also surprised me every time this script  came to a fork in the road  it didn't just take the road less  traveled it left the road altogether  that made its way across country I  honestly didn't know where it would end  up but I was never lost never afraid  because vigil is a great storyteller  she's always in command of her narrative  always in command of her characters her  heroine is a chibok girl but vigil took  the courageous decision to make her one  who got away  and at first I wasn't sure about this  she's then trafficked as a child bride  and then the script becomes a  rip-roaring action story of a father  looking for his daughter but at last I  understand the importance of the courage  and the authentic voice because in  telling the story of the girl that got  away  she ends up telling us everything about  the girls that are still missing  they have no greater advocate an African  writer a beautiful script a courageous  writer my countryman vigil Chima  [Applause]  good evening  do I sound calm I'm not at all to make  matters worse I'm standing not next to  one celebrity but four Wow well I'm  gonna try not to embarrass myself or my  country I begin my thanks to miss a gay  herself indeed it is a greatest thrill  as a Nigerian to be introduced by  another Nigerian British though she may  be what are the odds thank you so much  for all those beautiful things you said  about me I mean I didn't recognize  myself at all but I would try and see  myself through your eyes a little story  about my involvement with the nickel in  2008 I had written what I thought was a  masterpiece it had power it had courage  it had all those things I thought  anybody would read it and see the  meaning of life in what I was trying to  do they didn't agree at all  he didn't even didn't even get to  quarterfinals the rejection was so  painful that I swore that said I'm done  with the nickel I'm never going to talk  to them ever again it was like a bad  breakup you know if you break up with a  guy you swear off guys for all eternity  I've moved on with my life and I mean  that was 2008 so fast forward to 2017  bring back girl is ready you know and I  it was a very simple story compared to  the one I wrote in 2008 it was simple  because I was gonna go off to Africa  immediately and shoot her but I got into  a small snag I wasn't able to raise the  funds to actually begin or even complete  the story in frustration I went knocking  on an old boyfriends door the nickel I  said well here I am back again I know I  swore but I can't just leave her sitting  there so I turned it in I promptly  forgot that I did  and I just I mean why not I mean you've  built a very tough skin of rejection  there's they can do nothing to me at  this point  so imagine imagine my shock and awe when  I started getting the notification this  script is really good they said  quarterfinals I said really  okay bye semifinal seriously I actually  went back and read the script to be sure  what are they talking about like really  this one and then lo and behold you know  I could not have anticipated that we  would be here tonight I could not have  anticipated that I would win I could not  have anticipated all that when he would  bring I mean I have people calling me  speaking to me as if I have a writing  career and nor could I have foreseen  that my words those words are being  spoken by mr. Vaughn by Miss embosser ah  by mr. Santoro and by mr. Shay had I  known that my words would come out of  your mouths literally I would have  agonized more with the dialogue I would  have struggled to make them more  profound and eloquent but as to that  there was no need you guys read so  beautifully I mean I I was transported  out of this vast room to the AMC theater  in Harlem where I watched my movies  thank you so much for taking the time  out of your very busy lives to honor us  with your craft now I want to give a  gratitude to my family there are three  in the audience my brother Ken who  bought a a new outfit for this evening I  call this guy all the time what do you  think would happen here what do you know  don't do that do not do that so he's my  story guru my son here 16 year old judo  be he is my true work-in-progress when  he learned that mom won he's like I knew  you would this is your year you've been  riding since I was born which is true  but he later I figured out why he was  saying that he asked me so how much of  the prize do I get  you forget that your entire room and  board for life you owe me bro my my  auntie is here from Connecticut  she let me tell you what this woman did  upon learning that I I had won she took  it upon herself to call family she said  our vigil has won a very important award  and they said what kind of award she  said he's so important it's like she won  the Oscar ah the person screamed and  called somebody else substituted the  word like the Oscar for our vigil has  been nominated for an Oscar that person  screamed even louder I picked up the  phone and called a third person and now  said our vigil has won the Oscar in  screenwriting all over the world and in  the village all the Chima is roared even  those I'm not related to family and I  have street cred you know because of  this award so I am so thrilled in the  audience I want to say it I have some  supporters these are women screenwriters  over 40 yes I know I don't look it but I  am actually a woman screenwriter over 40  I met these ladies at the writers lab  retreat not too long ago ladies you're  in the house please let's make some  noise this is our moment so I win this  award not just for me but for all of us  but I will keep the money thank you  and finally finally the greatest thanks  I reserve to the Academy I mean I have  to I can't leave the stage without  saying thank you to the Academy to Don  and Gina Co who saw the need and the  vision to create this fellowship in 1986  85 to the army of readers who were able  to indeed with all seven thousand  entries into ten to the committee that  did have a spirited from what I hear  discussion to choose from that ten to  five they put this entire week together  and this evening and that's not all  consider that they paid for my flight  from New York to here consider that they  put me in a plush hotel on Beverly Hills  considering that they gave me a stipend  to cover the expenses for this week and  this is not to mention the prize itself  through it all the team has been  exceptional in their support I mean  they're asking me is it vigil or vigil  is it chime or team a is it bubucaca or  bubucaca I mean who does this who does  this people who want to make sure that  this evening goes well you are the  greatest champion and committee of  writers anywhere and in short tonight  this entire experience has made me feel  truly as if I did win the Oscar so thank  you thank you

